title: Generals of the Republic
subtitle: Should the Jedi lead the Republic's armies?
tags: event
view-if: war and geonosis_seen and not war_begins_seen
max-visits: 1
priority: 4
new-page: true
face-image: img/ev_war.svg
on-arrival: war_begins_seen = 1

= Generals of the Republic

[? if clones > 0 : The Grand Army needs commanders, and the clones were bred to follow Jedi. ?][? if clones <= 0 : The Republic's patchwork forces need commanders. ?] [? if rc_chancellor : The Security Bloc proposes?][? if not rc_chancellor : The Chancellor proposes?] that Jedi Knights be commissioned as generals. Many Jedi are uneasy: they are keepers of the peace, not soldiers.

- @generals: Accept Jedi as generals.
- @advisors: Insist that the Jedi serve as advisors and peacekeepers, not commanders.

@generals
subtitle: The war will go better. The Order will pay a heavy price.
on-arrival: jedi_generals = 1; war_balance += 1

The Jedi become generals. Within a year, a tenth of the Order has died in battle, and the public begins to see the Jedi as soldiers.

@advisors
subtitle: The Order stays itself. The war will be harder.
on-arrival: jedi_generals = 0; war_balance -= 1; jedi_relation += 8; jedi_standing += 3; hawk_dissent += 4

The Senate keeps the Jedi out of the chain of command. They serve as negotiators, scouts and protectors of civilians. The Order is grateful. The Security Bloc is not.
